{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NiGXizsF722jL5YQSogCY3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException\\n\\nSince TRUNK-6799, AuthorizationAdvice and core's explicit privilege\\nchecks denied with Spring Security's AccessDeniedException rather than\\nAPIAuthenticationException. Code catching the old type stopped\\nrecognizing denials; webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST\\nanswered 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\\n\\nAPIAuthenticationException now extends AuthorizationDeniedException.\\nCore throws it again wherever it did before 3.0.0, and wherever a\\n@PreAuthorize or @PostAuthorize check names the missing privilege, so a\\ncatch on either type recognizes the denial. It stays deprecated in\\nfavour of AccessDeniedException, which every denial is.\\n\\nIt is no longer an APIException, so a module compiled against an earlier\\ncore whose bytecode treats it as one fails verification until rebuilt.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6823: Deny a failed isAuthenticated() with APIAuthenticationException too\\n\\n@PreAuthorize(\\\"isAuthenticated()\\\"), the migration guide's translation of a\\nno-value @Authorized, denied a logged-out caller with a plain\\nAuthorizationDeniedException where @Authorized throws\\nAPIAuthenticationException, so converting such a method changed what its\\ncallers catch. It now records the denial for\\nPrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager to report as AuthorizationAdvice does.\\n\\nTestInstallUtil throws APIAuthenticationException again, as before 3.0.0,\\nand the migration guide notes that the class is no longer an APIException.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2d32d20938e007f2f9bf8e3a3c946758d52d6bfe\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T14:03:20+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6826: Request paths with a trailing slash find no handler on core 3.0 (#6680)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6826: Serve /ws request paths with a trailing slash from the handler for the path without it\\n\\nSpring 7 has no option to match a handler mapping to a path with a trailing\\nslash, so /openmrs/ws/rest/v1/session/ found no handler on core 3.0, where\\n2.x served it. TrailingSlashFilter hands /ws requests ending in a slash to\\nSpring's UrlHandlerFilter, which trims it, and web.xml runs it ahead of\\nspringSecurityFilterChain so URL rules judge the path the handler is chosen on.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* TRUNK-6826: Name the filter that enforces URL rules and reuse the /ws mapping constant\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* TRUNK-6826: Say in the javadoc that the /ws servlet root is left as it is\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* TRUNK-6826: Leave a /ws request whose URI ends in two slashes to the firewall\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7ad155e529e41cb5700cf29a7890f2d08e72b0b7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T13:44:02+03:00\",\"message\":\"Return HTTP 500 for uncaught exceptions (#6643)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes #6640.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"085d24ca28913de746060914ba4c0305680c9321\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12T13:43:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6824: Request paths with a repeated slash fail with 500 on core 3.0 (#6673)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6824: Collapse repeated slashes in the request path before Spring Security\\n\\nTomcat normalizes the servlet path and path info but leaves getRequestURI()\\nraw. Spring's request path parsing requires the context path plus the servlet\\npath to start that URI, so a request like /openmrs//ws/rest/v1/visit failed\\nwith a 500: in DispatcherServlet before TRUNK-6799, and since then already in\\nSpring Security's ServletRequestPathFilter, ahead of FilterChainProxy. The O3\\npatient chart's visit history sends exactly that URL.\\n\\nRepeatedSlashFilter, mapped right after charsetFilter in web.xml, collapses\\nruns of slashes in the request URI, URL and context path, so everything\\ndownstream, URL rules included, sees the path the container dispatched on.\\nStrictHttpFirewall keeps its defaults: it still rejects a // that reaches it,\\nand encoded slashes, path parameters and dot segments as before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6824: Test that web.xml runs RepeatedSlashFilter before Spring Security\\n\\nThe fix depends on web.xml mapping RepeatedSlashFilter to /* ahead of\\nspringSecurityFilterChain. WebXmlTest, in the webapp module, parses the\\ndescriptor and fails if no filter declares RepeatedSlashFilter, or if its\\nmapping is removed, placed after springSecurityFilterChain's, narrowed\\nfrom /* or kept off REQUEST dispatches. The webapp module gets\\nopenmrs-test and the servlet API as test dependencies for it.\\n\\nRepeatedSlashFilter's javadoc no longer names the firewall as what rejects\\nencoded slashes, path parameters and dot segments:\\n/openmrs/ws;x=y/rest/v1/session and /openmrs/x/../ws/rest/v1/session still\\nfail with a 500 in ServletRequestPathFilter, as they did before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"83411b2f8a52325e867fccc223a54d6a6f701400\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T22:20:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6819: Start the JobRunr job server only once OpenMRS has started (#6654)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The background job server was started while its application context was\\nstill being created, so jobs could run before the context was ready. On\\njetty:run this logged \\\"EntityManagerFactory is closed\\\" for a job that ran\\nduring the context refresh after modules start, against the closed session\\nfactory of the context being replaced, and \\\"Task class ... not found\\\" for a\\nmodule's job that ran after the first, core-only refresh, before modules\\nwere loaded.\\n\\nThe server is now started by a SmartLifecycle once its context has finished\\nrefreshing and stopped before the context closes. The webapp defers that\\nstart until SchedulerService.onStartup(), which runs once modules have\\nstarted; contexts refreshed after startup start their server right away.\\n\\nThe webapp never closes its application context, so Context.shutdown() now\\ncalls SchedulerService.onShutdown() first, as it did before the move to\\nJobRunr, and JobRunrSchedulerService stops the job server there, before the\\nmodules and the session factory are shut down.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NK4kFG8qyevx9Bk9jWoEgS\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdDdZrB8Q5eMgej5FmRx4R\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZ92BDLHrn6xACczVMtSiR\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ab66a1e09c42bac462e49f2bbf53f586fb882697\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T21:57:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6820: Write the DWR document type when creating dwr-modules.xml (#6655)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"createDwrModulesXml wrote no document type at all, so a file it created\\ngave DWR no grammar to validate against, and Listener kept it that way\\non every restart. It now writes the document type Listener writes.\\n\\nThe moduleId attribute that dwr-modules.xml carries is declared in the\\nDTD that openmrs-contrib-dwr bundles (openmrs/openmrs-contrib-dwr#7).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FBB3ZQetWQqkHrZQk9US1C\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WAi8ZLEN3Jyz2qnoudY89K\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"07e8ea06f244de96907581535d4eff8dadbd0004\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:26:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6707: Implement full caching for Global Properties (#6598)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f39e8f277c9e070bcb06032428bf0cf8cc8cc27a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T21:26:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6702: Make UpdateFilter and InitializationFilter skip checks cheap after startup (#6434)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"645814dc2cbf8ac809d61a92949aa308d368db7e\",\"date\":\"2026-09-11T20:35:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6701: Avoid redundant per-request session attribute writes in OpenmrsFilter (#6555)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1d0fb13892759020f6bc0824a097518d546024eb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T13:45:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Reduce the overhead of the gzip filter (#6505)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1bd8778fc13247eb712a6cd7a949461cccdb6b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T07:58:28-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6662: Get unchanged password hashing working using Spring's interfaces (#6219)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit d58b63501b7fedd1e6b02981262d73122b967621)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b68355b3dd934c7d5be3708d6637dfae8f845ee5\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T11:26:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Switch to saner DaemonThread protection scheme (#6349)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a98728ff2e8a62d723470decc13bf444523d585b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T00:26:57+03:00\",\"message\":\"Keep the setup wizard closed when a configured database is unreachable (#6333)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Keep the setup wizard closed when a configured database is unreachable\\n\\nDatabaseDetective.isDatabaseEmpty caught any connection failure and\\nreported the database as empty. Both callers, Listener startup and\\nInitializationFilter, use that result to decide whether to present the\\nunauthenticated setup wizard, so a database-connectivity failure on an\\nalready-configured deployment reopened the wizard, exposing the stored\\ndatabase credentials in the rendered form and letting an unauthenticated\\nuser reconfigure and persist their own settings.\\n\\nOnly a genuinely unconfigured instance (no connection URL) is now treated\\nas empty on a connection failure; a configured instance that cannot be\\nreached is reported as not empty, so it fails startup with a connection\\nerror instead of reopening setup. Also stop the finally block from\\nreturning inside a close() failure, which could otherwise flip a\\nnon-empty result to empty.\\n\\nAdds a regression test that a configured but unreachable database is not\\nreported as empty.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Use String.isBlank() instead of trim().isEmpty() to avoid allocating a new string\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b13fb5e02042b54bd11758e708ffbf1a681355ae\",\"date\":\"2026-07-20T23:58:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"Hold UpdateFilter authentication state per session (#6329)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"UpdateFilter.authenticatedSuccessfully was an instance field on the\\nsingleton filter, so once any super user authenticated at the first step\\nof the database-update wizard the flag stayed true for everyone. A\\nconcurrent unauthenticated request could then POST straight to the\\nreview-changes step and run the pending database updates on the strength\\nof another user's login.\\n\\nMove the authenticated flag into the HttpSession so each session must\\nauthenticate for itself. The shared update-in-progress state is left\\nglobal on purpose so multiple super users can still watch one running\\nupdate. Updates the E2E helpers to session scope, makes resetRequest carry\\nthe session forward (a follow-up request is the same client), and adds a\\nregression test that a second session cannot reuse another session's\\nauthentication.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d992f1746c140dc2effaf78fc86443ac35309a3c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-20T23:48:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"Bind caller-supplied names as query parameters instead of concatenating (#6335)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Bind the program-attribute name as a query parameter\\n\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName assembled its native query by\\nconcatenating the attributeName argument straight into the SQL text. Bind\\nit as a named parameter (:attributeName) instead so the value is always\\nhandled as a literal attribute-type name and can never alter the query.\\nThe patient-id list stays inlined since those elements are ints.\\n\\nAdds a regression test that a name containing SQL control characters is\\nmatched literally and resolves no attribute type.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Bind the global-property name in FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue\\n\\nReplace the concatenated global_property lookup with a PreparedStatement\\nso the property name is always treated as a literal value rather than\\nbeing spliced into the SQL text.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue name binding\\n\\nGuards that the property name is matched literally: a name carrying SQL\\ncontrol characters resolves no property (returns null) instead of being\\ninterpreted as query text, which the earlier concatenated query allowed.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e7052745fb78802c8adcd7c1962f3525e7050b1e\",\"date\":\"2026-06-12T21:54:53+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6646: Env-var key normalization drops create_database_* / create_user_* credentials in scripted setup (#6145)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"949b8a177e825320b0d04108accf38fc48751ed3\",\"date\":\"2026-06-02T20:17:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6643: Initial setup with MariaDB Driver does not work (#6150)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"708c62c6a48d0e40bfce49289ae0de99f302a816\",\"date\":\"2026-05-26T23:04:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"Fix 404 on /openmrs/ welcome page when no UI module is installed\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The *.htm servlet mapping routes /index.htm to the openmrs\\nDispatcherServlet, but core has no handler for it - so accessing\\nhttp://localhost:8080/openmrs/ via `mvn jetty:run` returns\\n\\\"No endpoint GET /openmrs/index.htm\\\" instead of the static\\n\\\"Platform Running\\\" page.\\n\\nRegister a DefaultServletHttpRequestHandler scoped to the exact\\n/index.htm path at Integer.MAX_VALUE - 1 precedence. Legacyui's\\n/**/*.htm handler (order=100) still wins when installed, and other\\nunmatched URLs (e.g. REST API paths) still flow through Spring's\\nNoHandlerFoundException handlers rather than being silently\\nforwarded.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"04a4cea80c7165fdfeaeb293cee89628d8a46b9e\",\"date\":\"2026-05-26T16:35:30+03:00\",\"message\":\"Stub InitializationFilter.startInstallation in E2E tests\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"InitializationFilterE2ETest's wizard-complete tests submit the\\nwizardcomplete.vm page to filter.doPost, which calls startInstallation\\nand spawns a real InitializationCompletion background thread on the\\nshared executor. That thread runs the actual setup using\\nwizardModel's default MySQL connection values and eventually calls\\nContext.setRuntimeProperties(...), overwriting whatever the next test\\nclass set in its constructor.\\n\\nThe background thread is asynchronous, so it races with subsequent\\ntests: SchedulerConfig.dataSource() reads Context.getRuntimeProperties\\nat bean-creation time, and when it's clobbered by the wizard's\\ndefault values, JobRunr's storageProvider fails to open the H2\\nconnection with 'Wrong user name or password'. The race resolves\\ndifferently across JVMs (Java 25 happened to pass, Java 21 didn't),\\nwhich made it look like flakiness.\\n\\nMake startInstallation protected and override it in\\nTestableInitializationFilter so the wizard-complete tests still\\nexercise the page-navigation logic without spawning the real thread.\\nThis also reverts the alphabetical surefire runOrder added earlier,\\nsince the fix no longer needs a particular test order.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"fc64842c3ae0620e7eceffdcbf8a3aaa6f1ec782\",\"date\":\"2026-04-14T14:10:39-04:00\",\"message\":\"Fix spotless formatting\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"22a4bae33c93d5a235cac846a440940733a5ce42\",\"date\":\"2026-04-14T14:00:17-04:00\",\"message\":\"Fix admin_password_locked implementation\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":22}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56a69749-6372-4876-b9ad-0e16dd28c740","uuid":"df0e314c-0364-42a7-a940-c8606337b49d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:09:56.981Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException\\n\\nSince TRUNK-6799, AuthorizationAdvice and core's explicit privilege\\nchecks denied with Spring Security's AccessDeniedException rather than\\nAPIAuthenticationException. Code catching the old type stopped\\nrecognizing denials; webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST\\nanswered 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\\n\\nAPIAuthenticationException now extends AuthorizationDeniedException.\\nCore throws it again wherever it did before 3.0.0, and wherever a\\n@PreAuthorize or @PostAuthorize check names the missing privilege, so a\\ncatch on either type recognizes the denial. It stays deprecated in\\nfavour of AccessDeniedException, which every denial is.\\n\\nIt is no longer an APIException, so a module compiled against an earlier\\ncore whose bytecode treats it as one fails verification until rebuilt.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6823: Deny a failed isAuthenticated() with APIAuthenticationException too\\n\\n@PreAuthorize(\\\"isAuthenticated()\\\"), the migration guide's translation of a\\nno-value @Authorized, denied a logged-out caller with a plain\\nAuthorizationDeniedException where @Authorized throws\\nAPIAuthenticationException, so converting such a method changed what its\\ncallers catch. It now records the denial for\\nPrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager to report as AuthorizationAdvice does.\\n\\nTestInstallUtil throws APIAuthenticationException again, as before 3.0.0,\\nand the migration guide notes that the class is no longer an APIException.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2d32d20938e007f2f9bf8e3a3c946758d52d6bfe\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T14:03:20+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6826: Request paths with a trailing slash find no handler on core 3.0 (#6680)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6826: Serve /ws request paths with a trailing slash from the handler for the path without it\\n\\nSpring 7 has no option to match a handler mapping to a path with a trailing\\nslash, so /openmrs/ws/rest/v1/session/ found no handler on core 3.0, where\\n2.x served it. TrailingSlashFilter hands /ws requests ending in a slash to\\nSpring's UrlHandlerFilter, which trims it, and web.xml runs it ahead of\\nspringSecurityFilterChain so URL rules judge the path the handler is chosen on.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* TRUNK-6826: Name the filter that enforces URL rules and reuse the /ws mapping constant\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* TRUNK-6826: Say in the javadoc that the /ws servlet root is left as it is\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* TRUNK-6826: Leave a /ws request whose URI ends in two slashes to the firewall\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7ad155e529e41cb5700cf29a7890f2d08e72b0b7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T13:44:02+03:00\",\"message\":\"Return HTTP 500 for uncaught exceptions (#6643)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes #6640.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"085d24ca28913de746060914ba4c0305680c9321\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12T13:43:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6824: Request paths with a repeated slash fail with 500 on core 3.0 (#6673)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6824: Collapse repeated slashes in the request path before Spring Security\\n\\nTomcat normalizes the servlet path and path info but leaves getRequestURI()\\nraw. Spring's request path parsing requires the context path plus the servlet\\npath to start that URI, so a request like /openmrs//ws/rest/v1/visit failed\\nwith a 500: in DispatcherServlet before TRUNK-6799, and since then already in\\nSpring Security's ServletRequestPathFilter, ahead of FilterChainProxy. The O3\\npatient chart's visit history sends exactly that URL.\\n\\nRepeatedSlashFilter, mapped right after charsetFilter in web.xml, collapses\\nruns of slashes in the request URI, URL and context path, so everything\\ndownstream, URL rules included, sees the path the container dispatched on.\\nStrictHttpFirewall keeps its defaults: it still rejects a // that reaches it,\\nand encoded slashes, path parameters and dot segments as before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6824: Test that web.xml runs RepeatedSlashFilter before Spring Security\\n\\nThe fix depends on web.xml mapping RepeatedSlashFilter to /* ahead of\\nspringSecurityFilterChain. WebXmlTest, in the webapp module, parses the\\ndescriptor and fails if no filter declares RepeatedSlashFilter, or if its\\nmapping is removed, placed after springSecurityFilterChain's, narrowed\\nfrom /* or kept off REQUEST dispatches. The webapp module gets\\nopenmrs-test and the servlet API as test dependencies for it.\\n\\nRepeatedSlashFilter's javadoc no longer names the firewall as what rejects\\nencoded slashes, path parameters and dot segments:\\n/openmrs/ws;x=y/rest/v1/session and /openmrs/x/../ws/rest/v1/session still\\nfail with a 500 in ServletRequestPathFilter, as they did before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"83411b2f8a52325e867fccc223a54d6a6f701400\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T22:20:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6819: Start the JobRunr job server only once OpenMRS has started (#6654)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The background job server was started while its application context was\\nstill being created, so jobs could run before the context was ready. On\\njetty:run this logged \\\"EntityManagerFactory is closed\\\" for a job that ran\\nduring the context refresh after modules start, against the closed session\\nfactory of the context being replaced, and \\\"Task class ... not found\\\" for a\\nmodule's job that ran after the first, core-only refresh, before modules\\nwere loaded.\\n\\nThe server is now started by a SmartLifecycle once its context has finished\\nrefreshing and stopped before the context closes. The webapp defers that\\nstart until SchedulerService.onStartup(), which runs once modules have\\nstarted; contexts refreshed after startup start their server right away.\\n\\nThe webapp never closes its application context, so Context.shutdown() now\\ncalls SchedulerService.onShutdown() first, as it did before the move to\\nJobRunr, and JobRunrSchedulerService stops the job server there, before the\\nmodules and the session factory are shut down.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NK4kFG8qyevx9Bk9jWoEgS\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdDdZrB8Q5eMgej5FmRx4R\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZ92BDLHrn6xACczVMtSiR\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ab66a1e09c42bac462e49f2bbf53f586fb882697\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T21:57:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6820: Write the DWR document type when creating dwr-modules.xml (#6655)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"createDwrModulesXml wrote no document type at all, so a file it created\\ngave DWR no grammar to validate against, and Listener kept it that way\\non every restart. It now writes the document type Listener writes.\\n\\nThe moduleId attribute that dwr-modules.xml carries is declared in the\\nDTD that openmrs-contrib-dwr bundles (openmrs/openmrs-contrib-dwr#7).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FBB3ZQetWQqkHrZQk9US1C\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WAi8ZLEN3Jyz2qnoudY89K\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"07e8ea06f244de96907581535d4eff8dadbd0004\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:26:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6707: Implement full caching for Global Properties (#6598)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f39e8f277c9e070bcb06032428bf0cf8cc8cc27a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T21:26:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6702: Make UpdateFilter and InitializationFilter skip checks cheap after startup (#6434)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"645814dc2cbf8ac809d61a92949aa308d368db7e\",\"date\":\"2026-09-11T20:35:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6701: Avoid redundant per-request session attribute writes in OpenmrsFilter (#6555)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1d0fb13892759020f6bc0824a097518d546024eb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T13:45:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Reduce the overhead of the gzip filter (#6505)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1bd8778fc13247eb712a6cd7a949461cccdb6b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T07:58:28-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6662: Get unchanged password hashing working using Spring's interfaces (#6219)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit d58b63501b7fedd1e6b02981262d73122b967621)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b68355b3dd934c7d5be3708d6637dfae8f845ee5\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T11:26:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Switch to saner DaemonThread protection scheme (#6349)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a98728ff2e8a62d723470decc13bf444523d585b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T00:26:57+03:00\",\"message\":\"Keep the setup wizard closed when a configured database is unreachable (#6333)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Keep the setup wizard closed when a configured database is unreachable\\n\\nDatabaseDetective.isDatabaseEmpty caught any connection failure and\\nreported the database as empty. Both callers, Listener startup and\\nInitializationFilter, use that result to decide whether to present the\\nunauthenticated setup wizard, so a database-connectivity failure on an\\nalready-configured deployment reopened the wizard, exposing the stored\\ndatabase credentials in the rendered form and letting an unauthenticated\\nuser reconfigure and persist their own settings.\\n\\nOnly a genuinely unconfigured instance (no connection URL) is now treated\\nas empty on a connection failure; a configured instance that cannot be\\nreached is reported as not empty, so it fails startup with a connection\\nerror instead of reopening setup. Also stop the finally block from\\nreturning inside a close() failure, which could otherwise flip a\\nnon-empty result to empty.\\n\\nAdds a regression test that a configured but unreachable database is not\\nreported as empty.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Use String.isBlank() instead of trim().isEmpty() to avoid allocating a new string\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b13fb5e02042b54bd11758e708ffbf1a681355ae\",\"date\":\"2026-07-20T23:58:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"Hold UpdateFilter authentication state per session (#6329)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"UpdateFilter.authenticatedSuccessfully was an instance field on the\\nsingleton filter, so once any super user authenticated at the first step\\nof the database-update wizard the flag stayed true for everyone. A\\nconcurrent unauthenticated request could then POST straight to the\\nreview-changes step and run the pending database updates on the strength\\nof another user's login.\\n\\nMove the authenticated flag into the HttpSession so each session must\\nauthenticate for itself. The shared update-in-progress state is left\\nglobal on purpose so multiple super users can still watch one running\\nupdate. Updates the E2E helpers to session scope, makes resetRequest carry\\nthe session forward (a follow-up request is the same client), and adds a\\nregression test that a second session cannot reuse another session's\\nauthentication.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d992f1746c140dc2effaf78fc86443ac35309a3c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-20T23:48:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"Bind caller-supplied names as query parameters instead of concatenating (#6335)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Bind the program-attribute name as a query parameter\\n\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName assembled its native query by\\nconcatenating the attributeName argument straight into the SQL text. Bind\\nit as a named parameter (:attributeName) instead so the value is always\\nhandled as a literal attribute-type name and can never alter the query.\\nThe patient-id list stays inlined since those elements are ints.\\n\\nAdds a regression test that a name containing SQL control characters is\\nmatched literally and resolves no attribute type.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Bind the global-property name in FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue\\n\\nReplace the concatenated global_property lookup with a PreparedStatement\\nso the property name is always treated as a literal value rather than\\nbeing spliced into the SQL text.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue name binding\\n\\nGuards that the property name is matched literally: a name carrying SQL\\ncontrol characters resolves no property (returns null) instead of being\\ninterpreted as query text, which the earlier concatenated query allowed.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e7052745fb78802c8adcd7c1962f3525e7050b1e\",\"date\":\"2026-06-12T21:54:53+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6646: Env-var key normalization drops create_database_* / create_user_* credentials in scripted setup (#6145)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"949b8a177e825320b0d04108accf38fc48751ed3\",\"date\":\"2026-06-02T20:17:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6643: Initial setup with MariaDB Driver does not work (#6150)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"708c62c6a48d0e40bfce49289ae0de99f302a816\",\"date\":\"2026-05-26T23:04:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"Fix 404 on /openmrs/ welcome page when no UI module is installed\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The *.htm servlet mapping routes /index.htm to the openmrs\\nDispatcherServlet, but core has no handler for it - so accessing\\nhttp://localhost:8080/openmrs/ via `mvn jetty:run` returns\\n\\\"No endpoint GET /openmrs/index.htm\\\" instead of the static\\n\\\"Platform Running\\\" page.\\n\\nRegister a DefaultServletHttpRequestHandler scoped to the exact\\n/index.htm path at Integer.MAX_VALUE - 1 precedence. Legacyui's\\n/**/*.htm handler (order=100) still wins when installed, and other\\nunmatched URLs (e.g. REST API paths) still flow through Spring's\\nNoHandlerFoundException handlers rather than being silently\\nforwarded.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"04a4cea80c7165fdfeaeb293cee89628d8a46b9e\",\"date\":\"2026-05-26T16:35:30+03:00\",\"message\":\"Stub InitializationFilter.startInstallation in E2E tests\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"InitializationFilterE2ETest's wizard-complete tests submit the\\nwizardcomplete.vm page to filter.doPost, which calls startInstallation\\nand spawns a real InitializationCompletion background thread on the\\nshared executor. That thread runs the actual setup using\\nwizardModel's default MySQL connection values and eventually calls\\nContext.setRuntimeProperties(...), overwriting whatever the next test\\nclass set in its constructor.\\n\\nThe background thread is asynchronous, so it races with subsequent\\ntests: SchedulerConfig.dataSource() reads Context.getRuntimeProperties\\nat bean-creation time, and when it's clobbered by the wizard's\\ndefault values, JobRunr's storageProvider fails to open the H2\\nconnection with 'Wrong user name or password'. The race resolves\\ndifferently across JVMs (Java 25 happened to pass, Java 21 didn't),\\nwhich made it look like flakiness.\\n\\nMake startInstallation protected and override it in\\nTestableInitializationFilter so the wizard-complete tests still\\nexercise the page-navigation logic without spawning the real thread.\\nThis also reverts the alphabetical surefire runOrder added earlier,\\nsince the fix no longer needs a particular test order.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"fc64842c3ae0620e7eceffdcbf8a3aaa6f1ec782\",\"date\":\"2026-04-14T14:10:39-04:00\",\"message\":\"Fix spotless formatting\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"22a4bae33c93d5a235cac846a440940733a5ce42\",\"date\":\"2026-04-14T14:00:17-04:00\",\"message\":\"Fix admin_password_locked implementation\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":22}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NiGXizsF722jL5YQSogCY3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
