{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017U6P8wvNUfVvU33XP7tdzA","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"085d24ca28913de746060914ba4c0305680c9321\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12T13:43:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6824: Request paths with a repeated slash fail with 500 on core 3.0 (#6673)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6824: Collapse repeated slashes in the request path before Spring Security\\n\\nTomcat normalizes the servlet path and path info but leaves getRequestURI()\\nraw. Spring's request path parsing requires the context path plus the servlet\\npath to start that URI, so a request like /openmrs//ws/rest/v1/visit failed\\nwith a 500: in DispatcherServlet before TRUNK-6799, and since then already in\\nSpring Security's ServletRequestPathFilter, ahead of FilterChainProxy. The O3\\npatient chart's visit history sends exactly that URL.\\n\\nRepeatedSlashFilter, mapped right after charsetFilter in web.xml, collapses\\nruns of slashes in the request URI, URL and context path, so everything\\ndownstream, URL rules included, sees the path the container dispatched on.\\nStrictHttpFirewall keeps its defaults: it still rejects a // that reaches it,\\nand encoded slashes, path parameters and dot segments as before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6824: Test that web.xml runs RepeatedSlashFilter before Spring Security\\n\\nThe fix depends on web.xml mapping RepeatedSlashFilter to /* ahead of\\nspringSecurityFilterChain. WebXmlTest, in the webapp module, parses the\\ndescriptor and fails if no filter declares RepeatedSlashFilter, or if its\\nmapping is removed, placed after springSecurityFilterChain's, narrowed\\nfrom /* or kept off REQUEST dispatches. The webapp module gets\\nopenmrs-test and the servlet API as test dependencies for it.\\n\\nRepeatedSlashFilter's javadoc no longer names the firewall as what rejects\\nencoded slashes, path parameters and dot segments:\\n/openmrs/ws;x=y/rest/v1/session and /openmrs/x/../ws/rest/v1/session still\\nfail with a 500 in ServletRequestPathFilter, as they did before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":2}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56a69749-6372-4876-b9ad-0e16dd28c740","uuid":"6111699f-9391-4a16-b17d-bf2dcc1f11f4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:10:30.250Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"085d24ca28913de746060914ba4c0305680c9321\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12T13:43:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6824: Request paths with a repeated slash fail with 500 on core 3.0 (#6673)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6824: Collapse repeated slashes in the request path before Spring Security\\n\\nTomcat normalizes the servlet path and path info but leaves getRequestURI()\\nraw. Spring's request path parsing requires the context path plus the servlet\\npath to start that URI, so a request like /openmrs//ws/rest/v1/visit failed\\nwith a 500: in DispatcherServlet before TRUNK-6799, and since then already in\\nSpring Security's ServletRequestPathFilter, ahead of FilterChainProxy. The O3\\npatient chart's visit history sends exactly that URL.\\n\\nRepeatedSlashFilter, mapped right after charsetFilter in web.xml, collapses\\nruns of slashes in the request URI, URL and context path, so everything\\ndownstream, URL rules included, sees the path the container dispatched on.\\nStrictHttpFirewall keeps its defaults: it still rejects a // that reaches it,\\nand encoded slashes, path parameters and dot segments as before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6824: Test that web.xml runs RepeatedSlashFilter before Spring Security\\n\\nThe fix depends on web.xml mapping RepeatedSlashFilter to /* ahead of\\nspringSecurityFilterChain. WebXmlTest, in the webapp module, parses the\\ndescriptor and fails if no filter declares RepeatedSlashFilter, or if its\\nmapping is removed, placed after springSecurityFilterChain's, narrowed\\nfrom /* or kept off REQUEST dispatches. The webapp module gets\\nopenmrs-test and the servlet API as test dependencies for it.\\n\\nRepeatedSlashFilter's javadoc no longer names the firewall as what rejects\\nencoded slashes, path parameters and dot segments:\\n/openmrs/ws;x=y/rest/v1/session and /openmrs/x/../ws/rest/v1/session still\\nfail with a 500 in ServletRequestPathFilter, as they did before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":2}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017U6P8wvNUfVvU33XP7tdzA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
